WEBVTT

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.530
Hey, now. Knock it off.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.900
You open that window, and you'll get a face full of smoke.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.620
Oh, c'mon! Don't be such a stiff!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:40.370
You're as stiff as this window.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.330
Hey, hey, Joe!

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.750
There's no need to rush!

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.210
It's not like we have any destination in mind.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:30.670
Yeah.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.500
And look over there.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.010
Look at how small the station seems.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.480
You're an odd one, all right.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.510
We don't get breaks often.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.480
We could've slept at an inn somewhere.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.650
But instead you stop at some random little station,

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.610
and as soon as we're off the train, we're climbing mountains.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.030
Yeah.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:54.980
Look at that, Ina-chan!

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.610
Look, it's the sea!

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.280
There's a steamer, too! You can see the steam!

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:24.010
So, you wanna go climb a little higher, Cap'n?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.870
Well, sounds like you're enjoying the mountain air.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.170
So, you wanna start heading down? We don't wanna be caught up here at sundown.

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.920
How long do you think it'll take to get over there?

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:21.470
Hey, Ina-chan! How long do you think it'll take to get up to that peak?

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.430
I don't think it's that far!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.850
We've already come this far!

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:34.560
Let's make it up there!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.650
Damn, this is some thick mist!

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.700
I think we got ourselves lost.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:52.420
The sun's about to set, too.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.520
Sorry for getting you lost in here, Ina-chan.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.360
That's good!

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:26.570
With this white mist around me,

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.790
it feels like I'm drinking in heaven, or paradise.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.910
Hey, Joe! Where are you going?

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.920
You just stay put and keep drinking!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.300
I'm gonna find a place to camp before it gets dark.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:47.800
Camp, huh?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.800
This almost reminds me of when I was a kid.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:57.390
Joe!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.300
Oh, you're awake already?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.390
Here she is, Joe.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.300
She's the one who saved you after you fell off the cliff.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.810
The name's Yuri. Nice to meet you.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:56.830
Here, Inaba-san.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.500
Just boil and drink it.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.960
It's a medicinal herb for healing bruises.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.040
I'll be taking care of the cattle if you need me.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.840
Man, what a girl!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.300
She sure works fast, I tell you.

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:15.930
Yeah.

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:18.180
What's the matter, Joe?

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.310
Your head still fuzzy from the fall?

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.940
Oh, no. That's not it.

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.480
I'm just gonna go wash my fa-

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.090
So she runs this farm alone with her mother?

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.420
That must be rough.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.140
But she said her mother is out on business.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.810
She's been running this place herself all month.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.680
Just try not to give her too much trouble.

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.270
Like you usually do, I mean.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.310
Hey, you don't have to put it like <i>that</i>!

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.810
Well, not like you'd be up to anything with your foot like that.{'up for any mischief'}

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.410
Anyway, I don't want the touring guys to worry.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.870
So I'll be heading back ahead of you.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.140
Remember, take it easy on your foot. Give it time to heal. {added long lead-out to match the fade-out - ninja}

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:28.900
A boxer's feet are his life.{same thing here - ninja}

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.680
Tough luck, you getting injured.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.270
This is the first time in a while I've done something like this.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.390
It's been fun.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:47.610
Later.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.600
Hey! Hey!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.200
Hey, you shouldn't be out here yet!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.410
That's cold!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:11:02.890
<i>When the roses blossom on the cape of Shiretoko...</i>

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:13.360
<i>Please remember us...{koku: and this is supposed to be Teruhiko Aoi, one of The Johnnys}</i>

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:23.950
<i>When we drank and made merry, and climbed the hill...</i>

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:56.400
Yasuo!

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.860
Is that you, Yasuo?

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.070
Yasuo! It's me, your mother!

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:09.710
Mother?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:36.060
Joe! Dinner's ready!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.690
Come and get it!

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.030
Huh?

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.070
Mother!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.650
Welcome home!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.320
Hi!

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:59.800
Cut it out, Yuri!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:00.760
It's just...

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.760
Even if they <i>are</i> the same age,

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.220
I can't believe you confused Joe for my brother Yasuo!

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:07.850
My eyes haven't been what they used to be.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.270
I'm getting old, I guess.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.430
I'm very sorry about that, Yabuki-san.

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.480
Well, I knew right away that you got the wrong guy.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:23.440
That's because I don't remember who my mother was.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:01.520
<i>Joe!</i>

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:06.530
<i>Joe! It's me!</i>

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.530
<i>It's me, Joe!</i>

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.620
<i>Joe!</i>

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:12.330
<i>Mommy!</i>

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:14.830
<i>Joe!</i>

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.830
<i>Mommy!</i>

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.330
<i>Joe!</i>

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.340
<i>Mommy!</i>

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.330
<i>Joe!</i>

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.420
<i>Mommy!</i>

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.340
<i>Joe!</i>

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:29.390
<i>Mommy!</i>

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:33.260
Mommy...{not sure if this should be 'mom' or just 'ma' throughout}

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.590
Are you really all right?

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.840
I'll be just fine!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.890
It doesn't hurt one bit!

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.390
Heave-ho!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:16.720
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.230
And-a hup!

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:29.200
Yabuki-san!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.280
If you have anything that needs mending, bring it to me.

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:35.280
Really?

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.670
I'll bring it right away!

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:46.840
There's some underwear in here. You don't mind?

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.800
It's all right. Give it to me.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.800
Thanks a lot!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:15:59.940
Oh, my bad.

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.230
Yabuki-san...

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:06.110
Are those boxing gloves yours?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.110
Yeah.

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:09.950
I see.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:34.340
You really remind me of my brother Yasuo when you do that.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.100
He hasn't been home in three years now...

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.100
But he used to work hard with Mother and me, day after day, just like you're doing, Joe.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.320
Then one day, he got up and left.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.360
He didn't want to stay out here in the countryside.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:55.120
He wanted to go to Tokyo and make money as a professional boxer.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:01.330
But that caused him to go astray.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.130
He hasn't even sent any letters.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:10.020
Ever since my brother left, my mother goes blank whenever she hears the word "boxing."

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:13.590
She wanted me to apologize to you for her.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.210
And she wanted you to stay as long as you can.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.680
I feel the same.

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:24.520
If you...

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.780
If you...

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:34.950
If you could become my brother...

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.030
I'd be very happy!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.480
Found it, Bro!{not 'boss' since they're just theives, not yakuza}

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:14.070
Good.

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:16.990
Gotcha!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:17.740
Wait!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.240
We need that money to buy cattle!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.450
Shut up!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:28.710
No point in screaming!

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:32.630
We know there's no one up here but you two!

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:34.970
Got it.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:52.570
A lone house in the mountains,{}{}

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.150
where a mother and her daughter live alone.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.860
I bet you thought it'd be an easy score...

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.240
You stupid thieves.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:03.790
Unfortunately for you, an incredibly strapping young lad has made a stop at this ranch.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.160
Get him!

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.160
It's go time!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.880
Son of a...

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:27.810
Well, there you have it.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.690
You get it?

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.030
Don't do it!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:52.710
Dammit!

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:53.250
Take this!

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.020
You bastard!

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.020
Wait!

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:08.260
Yabuki-san, please don't hurt him any more!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:11.270
Please don't hurt him any more!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:16.900
What are you talking about, Mother?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:19.110
He tried to steal the farm's money...

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.030
Don't you recognize him?

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.200
No matter how much he's changed...

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.500
I could recognize him at first sight.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.960
No... That thief can't be...

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:37.170
What a stupid boy you are.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:40.590
Who goes to steal from his own home?

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:44.560
Here. Take it with you.

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.300
You need money, don't you?

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:51.350
I don't know what you're doing for a living these days,

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:55.350
but I'm just glad to see you well.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.040
It really is you, Yasuo...

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.550
Out of my way, Yuri.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:31.550
Yasuo!

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.820
Mother!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:48.350
Mother!

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:50.580
Mother!

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.000
Yasuo!

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:05.970
I won't go anywhere anymore.

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:07.930
Thank you, Yabuki-san.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:09.520
I truly thank you.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:13.810
Thanks to you, we've gone back to the way things used to be.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:15.610
It's all thanks to you.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:20.440
Oh, it's nothing!

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:43.380
Sir, the train's almost here!

00:22:44.010 --> 00:22:45.220
I know, I know.

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:46.850
Just give me a minute.

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:51.520
Dear Madam and Yuri,

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:54.020
Sorry for leaving without saying a word.

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:58.430
I... I... uhh...

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:08.740
I really wanted to stay at the ranch myself,

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:12.910
but I thought it over, and there are things I need to take care of.

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:14.370
So this is goodbye.

00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:17.460
I'll come back to visit someday.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:19.750
I'll see you then.

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:23.670
P.S. To Yasuo-kun,

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.390
Take good care of your mother.

00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:44.210
Joe's life on the road continues, as he goes northeast to parts unknown.{"to unknown towns"}

00:24:44.210 --> 00:24:48.170
Meanwhile, Carlos visits the slum in Joe's absence,

00:24:48.170 --> 00:24:51.430
and after meeting with me and the kids, he gains an interest in Joe.

00:24:52.170 --> 00:24:56.680
At the Sendai Sports Center, where preparations are being made for the Carlos-Nango match,

00:24:57.890 --> 00:25:01.180
Joe and Carlos meet by chance.

00:25:01.810 --> 00:25:06.110
Now, as Joe clashes with the uncrowned emperor, Carlos,

00:25:06.110 --> 00:25:08.110
which way is tomorrow!?
